    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lineup today is anchored by **Gunnar Henderson**, whose matchup against Kremer yields an elite efficiency score of 79.74. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits significantly from a dynamic platoon advantage and the premium leadoff spot, making him our primary engine for R and RBI production. **Jacob Wilson** (65.32) and **Andy Pages** (63.46) also provide strong offensive output. **Andy Pages** is particularly intriguing; while facing a 4.08 xERA starter, he receives a notable boost from favorable wind conditions and the high-leverage context of batting second, which optimizes his chances to contribute across all five categories.\n\nWe continue to monitor the status of **Wade Meckler** (42.35) and **Liam Hicks** (52.88), both of whom are currently navigating \"Lineup Pending\" status. **Wade Meckler** presents a marginal start, as the left-on-left platoon disadvantage against Gore suppresses his projection, though his elite sprint speed keeps him in the conversation for our critical SB needs. **Drake Baldwin** faces an elevated risk profile with a 37% rain probability, though his 54.36 score remains viable given his leadoff positioning. **Jackson Merrill** (50.37) remains our most cautious start of the day; despite a high-upside platoon advantage, he is neutralized by the elite skill of Henderson, who holds a difficult 2.82 xERA.\n\nOur deepest bench decision centered on the margin between **Luis Lara** (40.41) and the rest of our reserve pool. **Luis Lara** barely cleared the threshold for a start despite a suboptimal #8 spot in the lineup, as we prioritize his roster flexibility over potential replacements like **Nasim Nunez** or **Heliot Ramos**. With **Kyle Tucker** and **Luis Robert Jr.** unavailable and **Jordan Westburg** still sidelined on the IL, we are forced to lean on our depth players to protect our daily game caps. We are proceeding with **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (60.95) in the #3 hole, trusting his baseline excellence to navigate the 3.83 xERA of Gray. We will continue to evaluate the availability of **Josh Jung**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Curtis Mead**, **Sam Antonacci**, and **Dominic Smith** as late-inning substitution options should the weather in **Drake Baldwin**\u2019s game force an early lineup shift.",
